# Daily/Weekly Summary Emails

> Personalized digest emails to re-engage users and celebrate progress.

**Priority:** P3 - Nice to Have
**Effort:** Low (1-2 weeks)
**Impact:** Re-engagement channel; user retention

---

## 1. Overview

### 1.1 What It Does

Automated personalized email summaries:

- Weekly wellness progress digest
- Streak celebration emails
- Gentle re-engagement for lapsed users
- Monthly outcome report summaries
- Achievement unlock notifications

### 1.2 Why It Exists

- **Re-engagement:** Email is a proven retention channel
- **Celebration:** Reinforce positive behaviors
- **Visibility:** Keep MindFriend top-of-mind
- **Low Friction:** Passive engagement without opening app

### 1.3 Success Metrics

| Metric             | Target | Measurement         |
| ------------------ | ------ | ------------------- |
| Email open rate    | 35%+   | Opens / Sent        |
| Click-through rate | 15%+   | Clicks / Opens      |
| Re-engagement rate | 10%+   | Lapsed users return |
| Unsubscribe rate   | <2%    | Unsubscribes / Sent |

---

## 2. Functional Requirements

### 2.1 Email Types

| Type               | Trigger                    | Frequency |
| ------------------ | -------------------------- | --------- |
| Weekly Summary     | Sunday 9am local           | Weekly    |
| Streak Celebration | 7/14/30/60/90/180/365 days | Event     |
| Achievement Unlock | Badge earned               | Event     |
| Lapsed User Nudge  | 3/7/14 days inactive       | Event     |
| Monthly Report     | 1st of month               | Monthly   |

### 2.2 Core Features

| ID    | Requirement                            | Priority |
| ----- | -------------------------------------- | -------- |
| SE-01 | Weekly progress summary email          | Must     |
| SE-02 | Streak milestone celebrations          | Must     |
| SE-03 | Lapsed user re-engagement              | Must     |
| SE-04 | Email preference management            | Must     |
| SE-05 | Unsubscribe with one click             | Must     |
| SE-06 | Personalized content based on activity | Should   |
| SE-07 | Achievement notification emails        | Should   |
| SE-08 | Monthly wellness report                | Should   |
| SE-09 | Deep links to specific app sections    | Should   |
| SE-10 | A/B testing subject lines              | Could    |

### 2.3 Email Preferences

| ID    | Requirement                     | Priority |
| ----- | ------------------------------- | -------- |
| EP-01 | Toggle all emails on/off        | Must     |
| EP-02 | Toggle individual email types   | Should   |
| EP-03 | Preferred send time             | Could    |
| EP-04 | Digest frequency (daily/weekly) | Could    |

---

## 3. Technical Requirements

### 3.1 Data Models

```sql
-- Email preferences
CREATE TABLE email_preferences (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE UNIQUE,

    -- Global
    emails_enabled BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,

    -- Individual types
    weekly_summary BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
    streak_celebrations BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
    achievement_notifications BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
    lapsed_nudges BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
    monthly_report BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,

    -- Settings
    preferred_send_hour INTEGER DEFAULT 9, -- 0-23
    timezone TEXT DEFAULT 'America/New_York',

    -- Secure unsubscribe token (RFC 8058 compliant)
    unsubscribe_token UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() UNIQUE,

    -- Unsubscribe tracking
    unsubscribed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    unsubscribe_reason TEXT,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Email send log
CREATE TABLE email_logs (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    email_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    subject TEXT NOT NULL,
    sent_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),

    -- Tracking
    message_id TEXT, -- From email provider
    opened_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    clicked_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    click_url TEXT,

    -- Status
    status TEXT DEFAULT 'sent', -- 'sent', 'delivered', 'opened', 'clicked', 'bounced', 'failed'

    -- A/B testing
    variant TEXT
);

-- Scheduled emails queue (with retry support)
CREATE TABLE email_queue (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    email_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    scheduled_for TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL,
    payload JSONB,

    -- Status
    status TEXT DEFAULT 'pending', -- 'pending', 'processing', 'sent', 'failed'
    processed_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    error_message TEXT,

    -- Retry tracking
    retry_count INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    max_retries INTEGER DEFAULT 3,
    next_retry_at TIMESTAMPTZ,

    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- Dead letter queue (permanent failures requiring manual review)
CREATE TABLE email_dead_letter_queue (
    id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT gen_random_uuid(),
    original_queue_id UUID REFERENCES email_queue(id),
    user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES auth.users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,

    email_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    scheduled_for TIMESTAMPTZ,
    payload JSONB,
    error_message TEXT,

    total_retries INTEGER,
    first_attempt_at TIMESTAMPTZ,
    final_attempt_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW(),

    requires_manual_review BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
    created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW()
);

-- RLS
ALTER TABLE email_preferences ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE email_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE email_queue ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE email_dead_letter_queue ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Users manage own preferences"
    ON email_preferences FOR ALL USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users view own logs"
    ON email_logs FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

CREATE POLICY "Users view own dlq"
    ON email_dead_letter_queue FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Service role can manage queue and DLQ
CREATE POLICY "Service manages queue"
    ON email_queue FOR ALL USING (true);

CREATE POLICY "Service manages dlq"
    ON email_dead_letter_queue FOR ALL USING (true);

-- Indexes for performance
CREATE INDEX idx_email_queue_scheduled ON email_queue(scheduled_for) WHERE status = 'pending';
CREATE INDEX idx_email_queue_retry ON email_queue(next_retry_at) WHERE status = 'failed' AND retry_count < max_retries;
CREATE INDEX idx_email_logs_user ON email_logs(user_id, sent_at DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_email_logs_type ON email_logs(user_id, email_type, sent_at DESC);
CREATE INDEX idx_dlq_review ON email_dead_letter_queue(requires_manual_review, created_at);
```

### 3.1.1 Timezone Calculation Function

```sql
-- Calculate user's local time in UTC for queue scheduling
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION calculate_user_send_time(
    p_user_id UUID,
    p_target_hour INTEGER,
    p_target_day_of_week INTEGER DEFAULT NULL,
    p_target_day_of_month INTEGER DEFAULT NULL
) RETURNS TIMESTAMPTZ AS $$
DECLARE
    v_timezone TEXT;
    v_user_tz TIMESTAMPTZ;
    v_utc_time TIMESTAMPTZ;
BEGIN
    -- Get user's timezone
    SELECT timezone INTO v_timezone FROM email_preferences WHERE user_id = p_user_id;
    IF v_timezone IS NULL THEN
        v_timezone := 'America/New_York';
    END IF;

    -- Start with today
    v_user_tz := NOW() AT TIME ZONE v_timezone;

    -- Adjust for weekly (day of week)
    IF p_target_day_of_week IS NOT NULL THEN
        -- 0 = Sunday, 6 = Saturday
        WHILE EXTRACT(DOW FROM v_user_tz) != p_target_day_of_week LOOP
            v_user_tz := v_user_tz + INTERVAL '1 day';
        END LOOP;
    END IF;

    -- Adjust for monthly (day of month)
    IF p_target_day_of_month IS NOT NULL THEN
        v_user_tz := DATE_TRUNC('month', v_user_tz) + (p_target_day_of_month - 1) || ' day'::INTERVAL;
    END IF;

    -- Set to target hour (00:00 in user's timezone)
    v_user_tz := DATE_TRUNC('day', v_user_tz) + (p_target_hour || ' hour')::INTERVAL;

    -- If time is in the past, move to next occurrence
    IF v_user_tz < NOW() AT TIME ZONE v_timezone THEN
        IF p_target_day_of_week IS NOT NULL THEN
            v_user_tz := v_user_tz + INTERVAL '7 days';
        ELSIF p_target_day_of_month IS NOT NULL THEN
            v_user_tz := v_user_tz + INTERVAL '1 month';
        ELSE
            v_user_tz := v_user_tz + INTERVAL '1 day';
        END IF;
    END IF;

    -- Convert to UTC
    v_utc_time := v_user_tz AT TIME ZONE 'UTC';
    RETURN v_utc_time;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;
```

### 3.2 Security Functions

```typescript
// Shared security utilities for email templates

export function escapeHtml(unsafe: string): string {
  return unsafe
    .replace(/&/g, "&amp;")
    .replace(/</g, "&lt;")
    .replace(/>/g, "&gt;")
    .replace(/"/g, "&quot;")
    .replace(/'/g, "&#039;");
}

export function escapeAttr(unsafe: string): string {
  return escapeHtml(unsafe).replace(/\//g, "&#x2F;");
}

// Helper to rate-limit emails to prevent spam
export async function checkRateLimit(
  supabase: any,
  userId: string,
  maxPerDay: number = 10,
): Promise<boolean> {
  const oneDayAgo = new Date();
  oneDayAgo.setDate(oneDayAgo.getDate() - 1);

  const { count } = await supabase
    .from("email_logs")
    .select("*", { count: "exact", head: true })
    .eq("user_id", userId)
    .gte("sent_at", oneDayAgo.toISOString());

  return (count || 0) < maxPerDay;
}
```

### 3.2.1 Edge Function: Send Email

```typescript
// supabase/functions/send-email/index.ts
// SECURITY: Uses token-based unsubscribe (RFC 8058), HTML escaping, rate limiting

import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts";
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2";
import { Resend } from "https://esm.sh/resend@1";
import { escapeHtml, checkRateLimit } from "./_shared/security.ts";

const resend = new Resend(Deno.env.get("RESEND_API_KEY")!);

interface EmailRequest {
  userId: string;
  emailType: string;
  subject: string;
  html: string;
  text?: string;
}

serve(async (req) => {
  const supabase = createClient(
    Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_URL")!,
    Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY")!,
  );

  const { userId, emailType, subject, html, text }: EmailRequest =
    await req.json();

  // Get user email and preferences
  const { data: user } = await supabase.auth.admin.getUserById(userId);

  if (!user?.user?.email) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "User not found" }), {
      status: 404,
    });
  }

  // Check preferences
  const { data: prefs } = await supabase
    .from("email_preferences")
    .select()
    .eq("user_id", userId)
    .single();

  if (!prefs?.emails_enabled) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Emails disabled" }), {
      status: 400,
    });
  }

  // Rate limit check: max 10 emails per day
  const withinLimit = await checkRateLimit(supabase, userId, 10);
  if (!withinLimit) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Rate limit exceeded" }), {
      status: 429,
    });
  }

  // Check specific email type preference
  const typeEnabled = {
    weekly_summary: prefs.weekly_summary,
    streak_celebration: prefs.streak_celebrations,
    achievement: prefs.achievement_notifications,
    lapsed_nudge: prefs.lapsed_nudges,
    monthly_report: prefs.monthly_report,
  }[emailType];

  if (typeEnabled === false) {
    return new Response(
      JSON.stringify({ error: "Email type disabled by user" }),
      { status: 400 },
    );
  }

  // SECURITY: Use unsubscribe token (RFC 8058 compliant) instead of plain userId
  const unsubscribeUrl = `https://getmindfriend.app/unsubscribe?token=${prefs.unsubscribe_token}`;

  // Send email
  try {
    const { data: emailResult } = await resend.emails.send({
      from: "MindFriend <hello@getmindfriend.app>",
      to: user.user.email,
      subject: escapeHtml(subject),
      html,
      text,
      headers: {
        // RFC 8058: One-click unsubscribe
        "List-Unsubscribe": `<${unsubscribeUrl}>`,
        "List-Unsubscribe-Post": "List-Unsubscribe=One-Click",
      },
    });

    // Log the email
    await supabase.from("email_logs").insert({
      user_id: userId,
      email_type: emailType,
      subject,
      message_id: emailResult?.id,
      status: "sent",
    });

    return new Response(
      JSON.stringify({ success: true, messageId: emailResult?.id }),
      {
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      },
    );
  } catch (error) {
    // Log failure
    await supabase.from("email_logs").insert({
      user_id: userId,
      email_type: emailType,
      subject,
      status: "failed",
      error_message: error.message,
    });

    throw error;
  }
});
```

### 3.3 Edge Function: Weekly Summary

```typescript
// supabase/functions/send-weekly-summary/index.ts

import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts";
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2";

serve(async (req) => {
  const supabase = createClient(
    Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_URL")!,
    Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY")!,
  );

  // Get users who want weekly summaries
  const { data: users } = await supabase
    .from("email_preferences")
    .select("user_id")
    .eq("emails_enabled", true)
    .eq("weekly_summary", true);

  if (!users) return new Response("No users", { status: 200 });

  const oneWeekAgo = new Date();
  oneWeekAgo.setDate(oneWeekAgo.getDate() - 7);

  for (const { user_id } of users) {
    // Gather user stats
    const [
      { data: profile },
      { data: moods },
      { data: quests },
      { data: exercises },
      { data: badges },
    ] = await Promise.all([
      supabase.from("profiles").select().eq("id", user_id).single(),
      supabase
        .from("moods")
        .select()
        .eq("user_id", user_id)
        .gte("logged_at", oneWeekAgo.toISOString()),
      supabase
        .from("quests")
        .select()
        .eq("user_id", user_id)
        .eq("status", "completed")
        .gte("completed_at", oneWeekAgo.toISOString()),
      supabase
        .from("exercise_sessions")
        .select()
        .eq("user_id", user_id)
        .gte("completed_at", oneWeekAgo.toISOString()),
      supabase
        .from("user_badges")
        .select("*, badges(*)")
        .eq("user_id", user_id)
        .gte("earned_at", oneWeekAgo.toISOString()),
    ]);

    const stats = {
      name: profile?.display_name || "Friend",
      streak: profile?.current_streak || 0,
      moodCheckins: moods?.length || 0,
      questsCompleted: quests?.length || 0,
      exerciseMinutes: Math.round(
        (exercises?.reduce((sum, e) => sum + (e.duration_seconds || 0), 0) ||
          0) / 60,
      ),
      badgesEarned: badges?.map((b) => b.badges.name) || [],
      avgMood: moods?.length
        ? (moods.reduce((sum, m) => sum + m.score, 0) / moods.length).toFixed(1)
        : null,
    };

    // Generate email HTML
    const html = generateWeeklySummaryHtml(stats);
    const subject = `Your week in review, ${stats.name} 🌟`;

    // ENQUEUE email send (queue-based architecture)
    // This ensures retry logic and rate limiting apply to weekly summaries too
    const { data: profile: userProfile } = await supabase
      .from("email_preferences")
      .select("preferred_send_hour, user_timezone")
      .eq("user_id", user_id)
      .single();

    const scheduledFor = calculateNextSendTime(
      userProfile?.preferred_send_hour || 9,
      userProfile?.user_timezone || "UTC",
    );

    await supabase.from("email_queue").insert({
      user_id,
      email_type: "weekly_summary",
      scheduled_for: scheduledFor,
      payload: { subject, html },
    });
  }

  return new Response(JSON.stringify({ processed: users.length }), {
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  });
});

function generateWeeklySummaryHtml(stats: any): string {
  return `
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <style>
    body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 0; background: #f5f5f5; }
    .container { max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto; background: white; }
    .header { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6); padding: 32px; text-align: center; color: white; }
    .header h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 24px; }
    .content { padding: 32px; }
    .stat-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 16px; margin: 24px 0; }
    .stat { background: #f8fafc; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px; text-align: center; }
    .stat-value { font-size: 32px; font-weight: bold; color: #6366f1; }
    .stat-label { font-size: 14px; color: #64748b; margin-top: 4px; }
    .streak { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #f59e0b, #ef4444); color: white; }
    .streak .stat-value { color: white; }
    .streak .stat-label { color: rgba(255,255,255,0.9); }
    .badges { margin: 24px 0; }
    .badge { display: inline-block; background: #fef3c7; color: #92400e; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 16px; margin: 4px; font-size: 14px; }
    .cta { text-align: center; margin: 32px 0; }
    .cta a { display: inline-block; background: #6366f1; color: white; padding: 14px 32px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
    .footer { padding: 24px; text-align: center; color: #94a3b8; font-size: 12px; }
    .footer a { color: #6366f1; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="header">
      <h1>Your Week in Review</h1>
      <p>Hey ${escapeHtml(stats.name)}, here's how you did! 🎉</p>
    </div>
    <div class="content">
      <div class="stat-grid">
        <div class="stat streak">
          <div class="stat-value">🔥 ${stats.streak}</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Day Streak</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-value">${stats.questsCompleted}</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Quests Completed</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-value">${stats.moodCheckins}</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Mood Check-ins</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-value">${stats.exerciseMinutes}</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Exercise Minutes</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      ${stats.avgMood ? `<p style="text-align: center; color: #64748b;">Your average mood this week: <strong>${stats.avgMood}/5</strong></p>` : ""}

      ${
        stats.badgesEarned.length > 0
          ? `
        <div class="badges">
          <h3>🏆 Badges Earned</h3>
          ${stats.badgesEarned.map((b: string) => `<span class="badge">${escapeHtml(b)}</span>`).join("")}
        </div>
      `
          : ""
      }

      <div class="cta">
        <a href="mindfriend://home">Continue Your Journey</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="footer">
      <p>You're receiving this because you signed up for MindFriend.</p>
      <p><a href="mindfriend://settings/notifications">Manage email preferences</a> | <a href="https://getmindfriend.app/unsubscribe">Unsubscribe</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
  `;
}
```

### 3.4 Edge Function: Lapsed User Nudge

```typescript
// supabase/functions/lapsed-user-nudge/index.ts

import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.168.0/http/server.ts";
import { createClient } from "https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2";

serve(async (req) => {
  const supabase = createClient(
    Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_URL")!,
    Deno.env.get("SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY")!,
  );

  const now = new Date();
  const threeDaysAgo = new Date(now.getTime() - 3 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);
  const sevenDaysAgo = new Date(now.getTime() - 7 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);
  const fourteenDaysAgo = new Date(now.getTime() - 14 * 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000);

  // Find users inactive for 3, 7, or 14 days
  const { data: inactiveUsers } = await supabase
    .from("profiles")
    .select("id, display_name, last_active_at")
    .or(
      `last_active_at.eq.${threeDaysAgo.toISOString().split("T")[0]},last_active_at.eq.${sevenDaysAgo.toISOString().split("T")[0]},last_active_at.eq.${fourteenDaysAgo.toISOString().split("T")[0]}`,
    );

  if (!inactiveUsers) return new Response("No lapsed users", { status: 200 });

  for (const user of inactiveUsers) {
    const daysSinceActive = Math.floor(
      (now.getTime() - new Date(user.last_active_at).getTime()) /
        (1000 * 60 * 60 * 24),
    );

    // Check if we already sent this nudge
    const { data: existingLog } = await supabase
      .from("email_logs")
      .select()
      .eq("user_id", user.id)
      .eq("email_type", `lapsed_nudge_${daysSinceActive}`)
      .gte(
        "sent_at",
        new Date(now.getTime() - 24 * 60 * 60 * 1000).toISOString(),
      )
      .single();

    if (existingLog) continue; // Already sent today

    const { subject, html } = generateNudgeEmail(
      user.display_name || "Friend",
      daysSinceActive,
    );

    await supabase.functions.invoke("send-email", {
      body: {
        userId: user.id,
        emailType: `lapsed_nudge_${daysSinceActive}`,
        subject,
        html,
      },
    });
  }

  return new Response(JSON.stringify({ processed: inactiveUsers.length }), {
    headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  });
});

function generateNudgeEmail(
  name: string,
  days: number,
): { subject: string; html: string } {
  const messages = {
    3: {
      subject: `We miss you, ${name}! 💜`,
      message:
        "It's been a few days since we've seen you. Even a quick mood check-in can help maintain your wellness journey.",
    },
    7: {
      subject: `Your streak misses you, ${name} 😢`,
      message:
        "A week has flown by! Let's get back on track together. Just one small step today.",
    },
    14: {
      subject: `Ready when you are, ${name} 🌱`,
      message:
        "Life gets busy, and that's okay. Whenever you're ready, we're here to support you.",
    },
  };

  const { subject, message } =
    messages[days as keyof typeof messages] || messages[14];

  const html = `
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Email Preferences - MindFriend</title>
    <style>
      * {
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }
      body {
        font-family:
          -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
        background: #f5f5f5;
        color: #1a1a2e;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        body {
          background: #0f0f1e;
          color: #f5f5f5;
        }
      }

      .container {
        max-width: 500px;
        margin: 40px auto;
        padding: 20px;
        background: white;
        border-radius: 12px;
        box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .container {
          background: #1e293b;
          box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
        }
      }

      .header {
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 32px;
      }
      .header h1 {
        font-size: 28px;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
      }
      .header p {
        color: #64748b;
        font-size: 14px;
      }

      .form-group {
        margin-bottom: 20px;
      }
      .form-group label {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        padding: 12px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        background: #f8fafc;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .form-group label {
          background: #334155;
        }
      }
      .form-group label:hover {
        background: #e2e8f0;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .form-group label:hover {
          background: #475569;
        }
      }

      .form-group input[type="checkbox"] {
        width: 18px;
        height: 18px;
        margin-right: 12px;
        cursor: pointer;
      }
      .form-group .label-text {
        flex: 1;
      }
      .form-group .label-text strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 2px;
      }
      .form-group .label-text small {
        color: #64748b;
        font-size: 12px;
      }

      .button-group {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 12px;
        margin-top: 32px;
      }
      button {
        padding: 12px 24px;
        border: none;
        border-radius: 8px;
        font-weight: 600;
        cursor: pointer;
        transition: all 0.2s;
      }
      .btn-save {
        background: #6366f1;
        color: white;
      }
      .btn-save:hover {
        background: #4f46e5;
      }
      .btn-cancel {
        background: #e2e8f0;
        color: #1a1a2e;
      }
      .btn-cancel:hover {
        background: #cbd5e1;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .btn-cancel {
          background: #334155;
          color: #f5f5f5;
        }
        .btn-cancel:hover {
          background: #475569;
        }
      }

      .unsubscribe-all {
        margin-top: 24px;
        padding-top: 24px;
        border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        .unsubscribe-all {
          border-top-color: #334155;
        }
      }
      .unsubscribe-all button {
        width: 100%;
        background: #ef4444;
        color: white;
      }
      .unsubscribe-all button:hover {
        background: #dc2626;
      }

      .success-message,
      .error-message {
        padding: 12px 16px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        display: none;
      }
      .success-message {
        background: #d1fae5;
        color: #065f46;
      }
      .success-message.show {
        display: block;
      }
      .error-message {
        background: #fee2e2;
        color: #991b1b;
      }
      .error-message.show {
        display: block;
      }

      .loading {
        opacity: 0.6;
        pointer-events: none;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="header">
        <h1>Email Preferences</h1>
        <p>Choose which emails you'd like to receive</p>
      </div>

      <div class="success-message" id="successMsg">
        ✅ Preferences saved successfully
      </div>
      <div class="error-message" id="errorMsg">❌ Error saving preferences</div>

      <form id="preferencesForm">
        <div class="form-group">
          <label>
            <input type="checkbox" name="weekly_summary" checked />
            <div class="label-text">
              <strong>Weekly Summary</strong>
              <small>Get your weekly wellness digest every Sunday</small>
            </div>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label>
            <input type="checkbox" name="streak_celebrations" checked />
            <div class="label-text">
              <strong>Streak Celebrations</strong>
              <small>Celebrate your milestones (7, 14, 30+ days)</small>
            </div>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label>
            <input type="checkbox" name="achievement_notifications" checked />
            <div class="label-text">
              <strong>Achievement Notifications</strong>
              <small>Get notified when you earn new badges</small>
            </div>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label>
            <input type="checkbox" name="lapsed_nudges" checked />
            <div class="label-text">
              <strong>Re-engagement Nudges</strong>
              <small>Gentle reminders if you've been away</small>
            </div>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="form-group">
          <label>
            <input type="checkbox" name="monthly_report" checked />
            <div class="label-text">
              <strong>Monthly Report</strong>
              <small>In-depth monthly wellness report on the 1st</small>
            </div>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="button-group">
          <button type="submit" class="btn-save">Save Changes</button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="btn-cancel"
            onclick="window.history.back()"
          >
            Cancel
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="unsubscribe-all">
          <button type="button" onclick="unsubscribeAll()">
            Unsubscribe from All Emails
          </button>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <script>
      const token = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get("token");
      if (!token) {
        document.getElementById("errorMsg").textContent =
          "❌ Invalid unsubscribe link";
        document.getElementById("errorMsg").classList.add("show");
      }

      async function loadPreferences() {
        try {
          const response = await fetch(`/api/email-preferences?token=${token}`);
          if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Failed to load preferences");

          const prefs = await response.json();
          document.querySelector('[name="weekly_summary"]').checked =
            prefs.weekly_summary;
          document.querySelector('[name="streak_celebrations"]').checked =
            prefs.streak_celebrations;
          document.querySelector('[name="achievement_notifications"]').checked =
            prefs.achievement_notifications;
          document.querySelector('[name="lapsed_nudges"]').checked =
            prefs.lapsed_nudges;
          document.querySelector('[name="monthly_report"]').checked =
            prefs.monthly_report;
        } catch (err) {
          console.error("Failed to load preferences:", err);
        }
      }

      document
        .getElementById("preferencesForm")
        .addEventListener("submit", async (e) => {
          e.preventDefault();
          const form = e.target;
          form.classList.add("loading");

          try {
            const response = await fetch(`/api/email-preferences`, {
              method: "POST",
              headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
              body: JSON.stringify({
                token,
                weekly_summary: form.weekly_summary.checked,
                streak_celebrations: form.streak_celebrations.checked,
                achievement_notifications:
                  form.achievement_notifications.checked,
                lapsed_nudges: form.lapsed_nudges.checked,
                monthly_report: form.monthly_report.checked,
              }),
            });

            if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Failed to save preferences");

            document.getElementById("successMsg").classList.add("show");
            setTimeout(
              () =>
                document.getElementById("successMsg").classList.remove("show"),
              3000,
            );
          } catch (err) {
            console.error("Failed to save:", err);
            document.getElementById("errorMsg").classList.add("show");
            setTimeout(
              () =>
                document.getElementById("errorMsg").classList.remove("show"),
              3000,
            );
          } finally {
            form.classList.remove("loading");
          }
        });

      async function unsubscribeAll() {
        if (
          !confirm(
            "Are you sure you want to unsubscribe from all emails? You can re-enable them anytime.",
          )
        ) {
          return;
        }

        try {
          const response = await fetch(`/api/email-preferences/unsubscribe`, {
            method: "POST",
            headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
            body: JSON.stringify({ token }),
          });

          if (!response.ok) throw new Error("Failed to unsubscribe");

          document.getElementById("successMsg").textContent =
            "✅ Unsubscribed from all emails";
          document.getElementById("successMsg").classList.add("show");
          setTimeout(() => (window.location.href = "/"), 2000);
        } catch (err) {
          console.error("Failed to unsubscribe:", err);
          document.getElementById("errorMsg").textContent =
            "❌ Error unsubscribing";
          document.getElementById("errorMsg").classList.add("show");
        }
      }

      loadPreferences();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
`;

  return { subject, html };
}
```

