## 6. Edge Cases & Error Scenarios

### 6.1 Zero Activity Handling

**Scenario:** User has zero mood check-ins, quests, or exercise activity.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Monthly report: Skip email entirely
- Weekly summary: Send minimal digest message
- Lapsed nudge: Still send if inactivity threshold met

**Implementation:**

```typescript
if (
  stats.moodCheckins === 0 &&
  stats.questsCompleted === 0 &&
  stats.exerciseMinutes === 0
) {
  continue; // Skip monthly report
}
```

### 6.2 Invalid/Expired Timezone

**Scenario:** User has invalid timezone string.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Fallback to UTC if lookup fails
- Log warning in Sentry
- Email still sends at UTC time

### 6.3 DST Transition Handling

**Scenario:** Email scheduled during daylight saving time gap.

**Expected Behavior:**

- PostgreSQL `AT TIME ZONE` handles DST automatically
- Email sent at next valid time
- User transparency maintained

### 6.4 Rate Limit Exceeded

**Scenario:** User earns 10+ badges in 1 hour.

**Expected Behavior:**

- First 10 emails sent today
- Remaining emails queued for tomorrow
- User notified of queue

### 6.5 Concurrent Queue Processor Collisions

**Scenario:** Two processors run simultaneously.

**Expected Behavior:**

- First acquires lock via `SELECT FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`
- Email sent exactly once

### 6.6 Webhook Signature Verification Failure

**Scenario:** Attacker spoofs webhook.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Server rejects with 401 Unauthorized
- No database changes applied
- Logged to Sentry

### 6.7 Resend API Rate Limits

**Scenario:** Resend returns 429 Too Many Requests.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Email marked as failed
- Retried via exponential backoff
- Moved to DLQ after 3 attempts

### 6.8 Database Connection Loss

**Scenario:** PostgreSQL connection drops mid-batch.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Partially processed emails already committed
- Remaining emails still pending
- Next cron run processes them
- No duplicate sends

### 6.9 User Unsubscribes During Send

**Scenario:** User clicks unsubscribe while email in queue.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Email send completes (already queued)
- `emails_enabled` set to false
- Next email skipped due to preference check

### 6.10 Invalid Email Address (Hard Bounce)

**Scenario:** Hard bounce received from Resend.

**Expected Behavior:**

- Webhook triggers email disabling
- User notified next login
- Prompted to update email address

---

## 7. Monitoring, Alerting & Observability

### 7.1 Email Send Tracking

**Metrics:**

- **Emails Sent:** Count of successful email sends
- **Delivery Rate:** Percentage of emails delivered
- **Open Rate:** Percentage of emails opened
- **Click Rate:** Percentage of emails clicked
- **Bounce Rate:** Percentage of emails bounced
- **Complaint Rate:** Percentage of emails complained about
- **Unsubscribe Rate:** Percentage of users unsubscribing

**Alerts:**

- **Delivery Rate < 80%:** Error rate too high
- **Bounce Rate > 5%:** Too many hard bounces
- **Complaint Rate > 2%:** Spam complaints increasing
- **Unsubscribe Rate > 3%:** Excessive unsubscribes

### 7.2 Error Logging

**Error Types:**

- **Rate Limit Exceeded:** User reached daily email limit
- **Invalid Email Address:** User entered invalid email
- **Email Service Down:** Resend API unavailable
- **Database Connection Failed:** PostgreSQL unavailable
- **Template Rendering Error:** Email content generation failed

**Error Handling:**

- **Rate Limit:** Email marked as failed, retried next day
- **Invalid Email:** User notified to update, email disabled
- **Service Down:** Email marked as failed, retried up to 3 times
- **Database Error:** Email marked as failed, moved to DLQ
- **Template Error:** Email skipped, user notified

### 7.3 Performance Monitoring

**Performance Metrics:**

- **Email Send Time:** Time to send email (should be < 1 second)
- **Email Delivery Time:** Time from send to delivery (should be < 30 seconds)
- **Email Open Time:** Time from send to open (should be < 1 hour)
- **Email Click Time:** Time from send to click (should be < 1 hour)

**Performance Alerts:**

- **Email Send Time > 2 seconds:** Email generation too slow
- **Email Delivery Time > 60 seconds:** Email send too slow
- **Email Open Time > 2 hours:** Users not opening emails
- **Email Click Time > 2 hours:** Users not clicking emails

### 7.4 User Engagement Tracking

**Engagement Metrics:**

- **Email Opens per Week:** Average number of email opens per user per week
- **Email Clicks per Week:** Average number of email clicks per user per week
- **Email Retention Rate:** Percentage of users who open emails
- **Email Click-through Rate:** Percentage of users who click emails
- **Email Engagement Rate:** Percentage of users who engage with emails

**Engagement Alerts:**

- **Email Opens per Week < 5:** Users not opening emails
- **Email Clicks per Week < 2:** Users not clicking emails
- **Email Retention Rate < 60%:** Users not staying engaged

---

## 8. Rollout Plan & Implementation Timeline

### 8.1 Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1-2)

**Objectives:** Build core infrastructure and data models

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Create database migrations (email_preferences, email_logs, email_queue tables with RLS)
- [ ] Implement PostgreSQL helper functions (calculate_user_send_time, etc.)
- [ ] Set up Resend/SendGrid account and API credentials
- [ ] Create base Edge Function structure and shared utilities

**Dependencies:** None
**Risks:** Database schema design impacts all downstream work

### 8.2 Phase 2: Core Functions (Week 3-4)

**Objectives:** Implement all Edge Functions

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Implement send-email function (rate limiting, preference checking)
- [ ] Implement send-weekly-summary function (digest generation, queueing)
- [ ] Implement send-monthly-report function (stats compilation)
- [ ] Implement lapsed-user-nudge function (3/7/14 day triggers)
- [ ] Implement process-email-queue function (batch processor)
- [ ] Implement retry-failed-emails function (exponential backoff)
- [ ] Implement email-webhook function (bounce/complaint handling with signature verification)

**Dependencies:** Phase 1 complete
**Risks:** Webhook signature verification requires careful testing; timing logic must be timezone-aware

### 8.3 Phase 3: Email Templates & iOS (Week 5-6)

**Objectives:** Create HTML templates and iOS UI

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Create Weekly Summary email template (responsive HTML with dark mode)
- [ ] Create Streak Celebration template
- [ ] Create Lapsed User Nudge template
- [ ] Create Monthly Report template
- [ ] Create Achievement Unlock template
- [ ] Implement unsubscribe web page (token validation, preference toggles)
- [ ] Implement Swift EmailPreferences model
- [ ] Implement SwiftUI EmailPreferencesView
- [ ] Add preferences to ProfileView navigation

**Dependencies:** Phase 2 complete
**Risks:** HTML email rendering across clients; timezone handling in iOS

### 8.4 Phase 4: Cron Jobs & Integration (Week 7)

**Objectives:** Wire up scheduled execution

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Set up 5 cron jobs (weekly summary, lapsed nudge, monthly report, queue processor, retry processor)
- [ ] Integrate email preferences API into iOS app
- [ ] Add deep links to email templates (mindfriend://)
- [ ] Web fallback configuration for email links

**Dependencies:** Phases 1-3 complete
**Risks:** Cron job timing; timezone database synchronization

### 8.5 Phase 5: Testing & QA (Week 8)

**Objectives:** Comprehensive testing and production readiness

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Unit tests for all Edge Functions (100% coverage on new code)
- [ ] Integration tests (database + functions + Resend)
- [ ] End-to-end testing (iOS app → Edge Function → email sent → webhook processed)
- [ ] Security testing (XSS, injection, signature verification)
- [ ] Performance testing (batch size, throughput, latency)
- [ ] Accessibility testing (iOS preferences UI)
- [ ] Manual testing (all email types, all timezones, dark mode rendering)

**Dependencies:** Phases 1-4 complete
**Risks:** Testing across multiple timezones; email client rendering variations

### 8.6 Phase 6: Monitoring & Launch (Week 9)

**Objectives:** Deploy to production and monitor

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Deploy all Edge Functions to production
- [ ] Enable cron jobs in production
- [ ] Configure Sentry alerts and dashboards
- [ ] Monitor email metrics (delivery rate, open rate, bounce rate)
- [ ] Gradual rollout (10% users → 50% → 100%) if needed
- [ ] Runbook documentation (common issues, troubleshooting)
- [ ] On-call rotation setup

**Dependencies:** Phase 5 complete
**Risks:** High email volume day 1; monitoring lag

### 8.7 Timeline Summary

| Phase                  | Duration  | Go/No-Go                   | Owner              |
| ---------------------- | --------- | -------------------------- | ------------------ |
| 1. Foundation          | Weeks 1-2 | Database tests pass        | Backend            |
| 2. Core Functions      | Weeks 3-4 | Function tests 100%        | Backend            |
| 3. Templates & iOS     | Weeks 5-6 | UI tests pass              | Frontend + Backend |
| 4. Cron & Integration  | Week 7    | E2E tests pass             | Backend + Frontend |
| 5. Testing & QA        | Week 8    | Security + Perf tests pass | QA                 |
| 6. Monitoring & Launch | Week 9    | Metrics dashboard live     | DevOps + Backend   |

**Total:** ~9 weeks to production

### 8.8 Go/No-Go Criteria

**MUST have before launch:**

- ✅ All Edge Functions tested (100% coverage on new code)
- ✅ All acceptance criteria met
- ✅ XSS, injection, signature verification verified
- ✅ Exponential backoff retry logic tested
- ✅ Timezone handling tested for DST transitions
- ✅ Queue processor tested for concurrent collisions
- ✅ Monitoring dashboards live
- ✅ Runbook documented

