## 8. Rollout Plan & Implementation Timeline

### 8.1 Phase 1: Foundation (Week 1-2)

**Objectives:** Build core infrastructure and data models

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Create database migrations (email_preferences, email_logs, email_queue tables with RLS)
- [ ] Implement PostgreSQL helper functions (calculate_user_send_time, etc.)
- [ ] Set up Resend/SendGrid account and API credentials
- [ ] Create base Edge Function structure and shared utilities

**Dependencies:** None
**Risks:** Database schema design impacts all downstream work

### 8.2 Phase 2: Core Functions (Week 3-4)

**Objectives:** Implement all Edge Functions

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Implement send-email function (rate limiting, preference checking)
- [ ] Implement send-weekly-summary function (digest generation, queueing)
- [ ] Implement send-monthly-report function (stats compilation)
- [ ] Implement lapsed-user-nudge function (3/7/14 day triggers)
- [ ] Implement process-email-queue function (batch processor)
- [ ] Implement retry-failed-emails function (exponential backoff)
- [ ] Implement email-webhook function (bounce/complaint handling with signature verification)

**Dependencies:** Phase 1 complete
**Risks:** Webhook signature verification requires careful testing; timing logic must be timezone-aware

### 8.3 Phase 3: Email Templates & iOS (Week 5-6)

**Objectives:** Create HTML templates and iOS UI

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Create Weekly Summary email template (responsive HTML with dark mode)
- [ ] Create Streak Celebration template
- [ ] Create Lapsed User Nudge template
- [ ] Create Monthly Report template
- [ ] Create Achievement Unlock template
- [ ] Implement unsubscribe web page (token validation, preference toggles)
- [ ] Implement Swift EmailPreferences model
- [ ] Implement SwiftUI EmailPreferencesView
- [ ] Add preferences to ProfileView navigation

**Dependencies:** Phase 2 complete
**Risks:** HTML email rendering across clients; timezone handling in iOS

### 8.4 Phase 4: Cron Jobs & Integration (Week 7)

**Objectives:** Wire up scheduled execution

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Set up 5 cron jobs (weekly summary, lapsed nudge, monthly report, queue processor, retry processor)
- [ ] Integrate email preferences API into iOS app
- [ ] Add deep links to email templates (mindfriend://)
- [ ] Web fallback configuration for email links

**Dependencies:** Phases 1-3 complete
**Risks:** Cron job timing; timezone database synchronization

### 8.5 Phase 5: Testing & QA (Week 8)

**Objectives:** Comprehensive testing and production readiness

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Unit tests for all Edge Functions (100% coverage on new code)
- [ ] Integration tests (database + functions + Resend)
- [ ] End-to-end testing (iOS app → Edge Function → email sent → webhook processed)
- [ ] Security testing (XSS, injection, signature verification)
- [ ] Performance testing (batch size, throughput, latency)
- [ ] Accessibility testing (iOS preferences UI)
- [ ] Manual testing (all email types, all timezones, dark mode rendering)

**Dependencies:** Phases 1-4 complete
**Risks:** Testing across multiple timezones; email client rendering variations

### 8.6 Phase 6: Monitoring & Launch (Week 9)

**Objectives:** Deploy to production and monitor

**Tasks:**

- [ ] Deploy all Edge Functions to production
- [ ] Enable cron jobs in production
- [ ] Configure Sentry alerts and dashboards
- [ ] Monitor email metrics (delivery rate, open rate, bounce rate)
- [ ] Gradual rollout (10% users → 50% → 100%) if needed
- [ ] Runbook documentation (common issues, troubleshooting)
- [ ] On-call rotation setup

**Dependencies:** Phase 5 complete
**Risks:** High email volume day 1; monitoring lag

### 8.7 Timeline Summary

| Phase                  | Duration  | Go/No-Go                   | Owner              |
| ---------------------- | --------- | -------------------------- | ------------------ |
| 1. Foundation          | Weeks 1-2 | Database tests pass        | Backend            |
| 2. Core Functions      | Weeks 3-4 | Function tests 100%        | Backend            |
| 3. Templates & iOS     | Weeks 5-6 | UI tests pass              | Frontend + Backend |
| 4. Cron & Integration  | Week 7    | E2E tests pass             | Backend + Frontend |
| 5. Testing & QA        | Week 8    | Security + Perf tests pass | QA                 |
| 6. Monitoring & Launch | Week 9    | Metrics dashboard live     | DevOps + Backend   |

**Total:** ~9 weeks to production

### 8.8 Go/No-Go Criteria

**MUST have before launch:**

- ✅ All Edge Functions tested (100% coverage on new code)
- ✅ All acceptance criteria met
- ✅ XSS, injection, signature verification verified
- ✅ Exponential backoff retry logic tested
- ✅ Timezone handling tested for DST transitions
- ✅ Queue processor tested for concurrent collisions
